# Response-template intents of the handlers issue #918 (R914-6) moved from
# compiled prose to seed responses. Each record names one `intent` key a
# multilingual-responses-*.lino file carries response records for, so the
# closure audit resolves the key to an authored definition rather than an
# open reference. The shape follows the localized_response_template records
# of data/seed/meanings-response-intents.lino.
meanings
  numeric_list_intro_sort
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a numeric-list request asks for code that sorts the list in ascending order"
    effect "the answer introduces the generated program with its language and the list as given"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Here is Python code that sorts the numbers 3, 1, 2 in ascending order:"
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-numeric-list.lino"
  numeric_list_intro_reverse_sort
    defined-by answer
